1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,197
Let us recap.

2
00:00:01,197 --> 00:00:07,161
An ether is R O R dash, an isomer of an alcohol, simple or mixed.

3
00:00:07,161 --> 00:00:10,026
The smaller group is named as alkoxy.

4
00:00:10,026 --> 00:00:11,888
Ethers show metamerism.

5
00:00:11,888 --> 00:00:18,776
Williamson's synthesis is an S N two reaction, so the bulky group must be the alkoxide.

6
00:00:18,776 --> 00:00:26,223
With no O H, ethers cannot hydrogen bond to each other and boil low, yet dissolve in water.

7
00:00:26,223 --> 00:00:33,489
The oxygen is a Lewis base: cold acids give oxonium salts, hot H I breaks both bonds.

8
00:00:33,489 --> 00:00:36,861
Anisole gives phenol and iodomethane.

9
00:00:36,861 --> 00:00:44,140
Old ether forms explosive peroxides, and chlorine replaces the alpha hydrogens first.

